# M1 -- operating a repository the other implementation created and populated.
#
# Two directions:
#   D1  created-by t, populated-by t, operated-by p
#   D2  created-by p, populated-by p, operated-by t
#
# Every cell carries one uniform postcondition in addition to its own outcome:
# after the operator finishes, the producing implementation still finds the
# repository valid, and its ref list and commit checksums are unchanged except as
# the operation intended.
#
# Operation tokens:
#   read-metadata          resolve a ref, read a commit, list refs, read history
#   read-content           list a tree, read file content
#   fsck                   verify object integrity and completeness
#   diff                   report changed paths between two commits
#   config-read            read the repository config
#   checkout-copy          check out a commit by copy or reflink
#   checkout-hardlink      check out a commit by hardlinking the objects
#   commit-into            add a new commit to the existing repository
#   refs-update            create, delete, or alias a ref
#   prune                  delete unreachable objects
#   summary-regenerate     rewrite the summary from the refs
#   sign-verify            sign a commit, and verify a signature the other made
#   static-delta-generate  generate a delta between two commits
#   static-delta-apply     apply a delta the other implementation generated
#   tar-export             write the commit tree as a tar stream
#   composefs-export       write the commit's composefs image
#   lock-exclusion         acquire the repository lock while the other holds it
#
# The corpus for M1 is C0 unless a record names another. Cells that depend on
# corpus content are covered in m0-content.matrix.
#
# Field reference and the outcome vocabulary are in README.md.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# D1 -- the tool creates and populates, the port operates.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

family: M1
created-by: t
populated-by: t
operated-by: p
op: read-metadata read-content fsck diff config-read checkout-copy
 checkout-hardlink commit-into refs-update prune summary-regenerate sign-verify
 static-delta-generate static-delta-apply tar-export composefs-export
 lock-exclusion
modes: bare-user-shared
tier: T0
outcome: impossible
severity: interop
identity: n-a
oracle: exit-status
evidence: -
spec: format-reference.md#port-extension-bare-user-shared-mode
note: The mode is a port extension. The tool rejects it when the repository is
 opened, so it can neither create nor populate one, and this column has no
 producer. The reverse direction is covered in D2 below.

family: M1
created-by: t
populated-by: t
operated-by: p
op: read-metadata read-content fsck diff config-read checkout-copy tar-export
modes: bare-split-xattrs
tier: T0
outcome: unobserved
severity: interop
identity: n-a
oracle: manifest checksum-agreement
evidence: ostrya::read_split_xattrs
spec: format-reference.md#bare-split-xattrs-mode
question: Establish first whether the tool can populate a repository in this mode
 at all, and by which gate. Its write support is experimental and gated. The
 port's read support is currently proven against hand-built objects rather than
 tool output, so the oracle for these cells does not yet involve the tool.

