# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# D2 -- the port creates and populates, the tool operates.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

family: M1
created-by: p
populated-by: p
operated-by: t
op: read-metadata read-content fsck diff config-read checkout-copy
 checkout-hardlink commit-into refs-update prune summary-regenerate sign-verify
 static-delta-generate static-delta-apply tar-export composefs-export
 lock-exclusion
modes: bare-user-shared
tier: T0
outcome: refused-clean
severity: interop
identity: n-a
oracle: exit-status stderr-text
evidence: -
spec: format-reference.md#port-extension-bare-user-shared-mode
note: Observed with ostree 2026.1. Every subcommand fails when the repository is
 opened, before the operation runs, with "error: opening repo: Invalid mode
 'bare-user-shared' in repository configuration" and exit status 1. The
 repository is left unmodified. The route to the tool for this mode is a port-run
 pull-local into a tool-readable mode; object identity is preserved by design so
 that the migration is lossless. That migration is a cell in m2-pull-local.
question: Add a test that pins this message and the exit status, so a future tool
 release that changes the refusal is caught.

